## 1️⃣  `code_to_string` – return a `std::string_view` and add a safe default case  

```cpp
// tf_status.hpp (or wherever TF_Code helpers live)

#include <tensorflow/c/c_api.h>
#include <string_view>

namespace tf {

[[nodiscard]] constexpr std::string_view code_to_string(TF_Code code) noexcept
{
    using namespace std::literals;               // enables the "sv" suffix
    switch (code) {
        case TF_OK:                 return "OK"sv;
        case TF_CANCELLED:          return "CANCELLED"sv;
        case TF_UNKNOWN:            return "UNKNOWN"sv;
        case TF_INVALID_ARGUMENT:   return "INVALID_ARGUMENT"sv;
        case TF_DEADLINE_EXCEEDED:  return "DEADLINE_EXCEEDED"sv;
        case TF_NOT_FOUND:          return "NOT_FOUND"sv;
        case TF_ALREADY_EXISTS:     return "ALREADY_EXISTS"sv;
        case TF_PERMISSION_DENIED:  return "PERMISSION_DENIED"sv;
        case TF_UNAUTHENTICATED:    return "UNAUTHENTICATED"sv;
        case TF_RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED: return "RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED"sv;
        case TF_FAILED_PRECONDITION:return "FAILED_PRECONDITION"sv;
        case TF_ABORTED:            return "ABORTED"sv;
        case TF_OUT_OF_RANGE:       return "OUT_OF_RANGE"sv;
        case TF_UNIMPLEMENTED:      return "UNIMPLEMENTED"sv;
        case TF_INTERNAL:           return "INTERNAL"sv;
        case TF_UNAVAILABLE:        return "UNAVAILABLE"sv;
        case TF_DATA_LOSS:          return "DATA_LOSS"sv;
        default:                    return "UNKNOWN_CODE"sv;   // future‑proof guard
    }
}
} // namespace tf
```

*Why this helps* – Returning `std::string_view` avoids hidden C‑string lifetime problems and the `default` arm guarantees a sensible result if TensorFlow ever adds new enum values.

