## 5️⃣  (Optional) `consume_status` as a **unique‑ptr** helper – single‑line alternative  

If you prefer a generic “own‑and‑delete” wrapper, you can use `std::unique_ptr` with a custom deleter:

```cpp
inline void consume_status_ptr(
    TF_Status* raw,
    std::string_view context = "",
    std::source_location loc = std::source_location::current())
{
    if (!raw) return;

    using StatusPtr = std::unique_ptr<TF_Status, decltype(&TF_DeleteStatus)>;
    StatusPtr guard{raw, TF_DeleteStatus};

    Status st{guard.get()};
    st.throw_if_error(context, loc);
}
```

Both versions achieve the same safety guarantees; pick the style that fits your code‑base.

